{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "ThreatForge",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/Krishita17/threat-forge",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "S-EXT-AUTHN",
              "name": "UnauthenticatedExternalActorCanImpersonateALegitimateUser",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unauthenticated external actor can impersonate a legitimate user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "End User is an external entity whose requests are not strongly authenticated, so an attacker can impersonate it (e.g. credential stuffing, forged identity)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/287.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Spoofing** against `End User`.\n\nMitigation: Require strong authentication for this actor (MFA where feasible), enforce password/credential policy, and rate-limit/lock out credential-stuffing attempts.\nControls: ASVS-2.1.1, NIST-IA-2, NIST-IA-5\nWeakness: CWE-287\nOWASP Top 10: A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "markdown": "**Spoofing** against `End User`.\n\nMitigation: Require strong authentication for this actor (MFA where feasible), enforce password/credential policy, and rate-limit/lock out credential-stuffing attempts.\nControls: ASVS-2.1.1, NIST-IA-2, NIST-IA-5\nWeakness: CWE-287\nOWASP Top 10: A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Spoofing",
                "cwe": "CWE-287",
                "owaspTop10": "A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "S-PROC-WEAKAUTH",
              "name": "ProcessAcceptsRequestsWithoutVerifyingCallerIdentity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Process accepts requests without verifying caller identity"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service handles requests but does not authenticate its caller, allowing a spoofed client to act as a trusted one."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/306.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Spoofing** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Authenticate every request to this process; reject or challenge unauthenticated callers at the trust boundary.\nControls: ASVS-2.1.1, NIST-IA-2\nWeakness: CWE-306\nOWASP Top 10: A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "markdown": "**Spoofing** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Authenticate every request to this process; reject or challenge unauthenticated callers at the trust boundary.\nControls: ASVS-2.1.1, NIST-IA-2\nWeakness: CWE-306\nOWASP Top 10: A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Spoofing",
                "cwe": "CWE-306",
                "owaspTop10": "A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures",
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "I-STORE-ATREST",
              "name": "SensitiveDataAtRestIsNotEncrypted",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive data at rest is not encrypted"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database stores sensitive data (credentials, pii) without encryption at rest, exposing it if the store is compromised."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/311.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Information disclosure** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt sensitive data at rest, manage keys separately from data, and restrict decrypt access to least privilege.\nControls: ASVS-8.3.4, NIST-SC-28\nWeakness: CWE-311\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "markdown": "**Information disclosure** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt sensitive data at rest, manage keys separately from data, and restrict decrypt access to least privilege.\nControls: ASVS-8.3.4, NIST-SC-28\nWeakness: CWE-311\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Information disclosure",
                "cwe": "CWE-311",
                "owaspTop10": "A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "I-FLOW-PLAINTEXT",
              "name": "SensitiveDataIsExposedInTransit",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive data is exposed in transit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database carries sensitive data (credentials, pii) across a boundary without encryption, so it can be intercepted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Information disclosure** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt the channel end-to-end; minimize sensitive fields in transit and avoid placing them in URLs or logs.\nControls: ASVS-9.1.1, ASVS-8.3.1, NIST-SC-8\nWeakness: CWE-319\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "markdown": "**Information disclosure** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt the channel end-to-end; minimize sensitive fields in transit and avoid placing them in URLs or logs.\nControls: ASVS-9.1.1, ASVS-8.3.1, NIST-SC-8\nWeakness: CWE-319\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Information disclosure",
                "cwe": "CWE-319",
                "owaspTop10": "A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "E-PROC-AUTHZ",
              "name": "MissingOrWeakAuthorizationEnablesPrivilegeEscalation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing or weak authorization enables privilege escalation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service does not enforce authorization checks per action, so an authenticated low-privilege actor may perform privileged operations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Elevation of privilege** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Enforce server-side, deny-by-default authorization on every privileged action; apply least privilege and verify object-level access.\nControls: ASVS-4.1.1, ASVS-4.1.3, NIST-AC-3, NIST-AC-6\nWeakness: CWE-285\nOWASP Top 10: A01:2021 - Broken Access Control",
                "markdown": "**Elevation of privilege** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Enforce server-side, deny-by-default authorization on every privileged action; apply least privilege and verify object-level access.\nControls: ASVS-4.1.1, ASVS-4.1.3, NIST-AC-3, NIST-AC-6\nWeakness: CWE-285\nOWASP Top 10: A01:2021 - Broken Access Control"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Elevation of privilege",
                "cwe": "CWE-285",
                "owaspTop10": "A01:2021 - Broken Access Control",
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DD-FLOW-DISCLOSE",
              "name": "PersonalDataIsDisclosedAcrossABoundary",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Personal data is disclosed across a boundary"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database carries personal data (credentials, pii) across a trust boundary, exposing it to parties that may not need it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Disclosure of information** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Share the minimum personal data necessary across the boundary; apply purpose limitation and a data-processing agreement for third parties.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-MIN, NIST-PT-3",
                "markdown": "**Disclosure of information** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Share the minimum personal data necessary across the boundary; apply purpose limitation and a data-processing agreement for third parties.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-MIN, NIST-PT-3"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Disclosure of information",
                "cwe": "",
                "owaspTop10": "",
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "I-STORE-IDENT",
              "name": "IndividualsAreIdentifiable(noDataMinimisationAnonymisation)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Individuals are identifiable (no data minimisation/anonymisation)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database retains directly identifying personal data without minimisation or anonymisation, increasing re-identification risk."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Identifiability** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Minimise collected fields, anonymise or aggregate where possible, and avoid storing direct identifiers you do not need.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-MIN, NIST-PT-3",
                "markdown": "**Identifiability** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Minimise collected fields, anonymise or aggregate where possible, and avoid storing direct identifiers you do not need.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-MIN, NIST-PT-3"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Identifiability",
                "cwe": "",
                "owaspTop10": "",
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "T-FLOW-NOTLS",
              "name": "DataInTransitCanBeTamperedWithAcrossATrustBoundary",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data in transit can be tampered with across a trust boundary"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database crosses a trust boundary without transport integrity (no TLS/encryption), so an on-path attacker can modify the data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Tampering** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt and integrity-protect the channel (TLS 1.2+); reject plaintext transport for any boundary-crossing flow.\nControls: ASVS-9.1.1, NIST-SC-8\nWeakness: CWE-319\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "markdown": "**Tampering** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Encrypt and integrity-protect the channel (TLS 1.2+); reject plaintext transport for any boundary-crossing flow.\nControls: ASVS-9.1.1, NIST-SC-8\nWeakness: CWE-319\nOWASP Top 10: A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Tampering",
                "cwe": "CWE-319",
                "owaspTop10": "A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures",
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "T-PROC-INPUT",
              "name": "UntrustedInputReachesTheProcessWithoutValidation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Untrusted input reaches the process without validation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service receives data from a less-trusted zone and may process it without validation, enabling injection or state corruption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Tampering** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Validate and canonicalize all input at the boundary; use parameterized queries and context-aware output encoding.\nControls: ASVS-5.1.3, ASVS-5.3.4\nWeakness: CWE-20\nOWASP Top 10: A03:2021 - Injection",
                "markdown": "**Tampering** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Validate and canonicalize all input at the boundary; use parameterized queries and context-aware output encoding.\nControls: ASVS-5.1.3, ASVS-5.3.4\nWeakness: CWE-20\nOWASP Top 10: A03:2021 - Injection"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Tampering",
                "cwe": "CWE-20",
                "owaspTop10": "A03:2021 - Injection",
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "E-PROC-ADMIN",
              "name": "Internet-facingPathCanReachPrivilegedAdminFunctionality",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Internet-facing path can reach privileged/admin functionality"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service is internet-facing and sits on a path toward trusted/admin functions; a flaw here can be leveraged to reach privileged operations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/269.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Elevation of privilege** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Segment admin functionality behind separate authentication and network controls; never expose privileged operations on the public path.\nControls: ASVS-4.1.1, NIST-AC-6\nWeakness: CWE-269\nOWASP Top 10: A01:2021 - Broken Access Control",
                "markdown": "**Elevation of privilege** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Segment admin functionality behind separate authentication and network controls; never expose privileged operations on the public path.\nControls: ASVS-4.1.1, NIST-AC-6\nWeakness: CWE-269\nOWASP Top 10: A01:2021 - Broken Access Control"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Elevation of privilege",
                "cwe": "CWE-269",
                "owaspTop10": "A01:2021 - Broken Access Control",
                "security-severity": "4.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "U-EXT-CONSENT",
              "name": "DataSubjectMayBeUnawareOfProcessing(noConsentSignal)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data subject may be unaware of processing (no consent signal)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "End User is a data subject whose awareness/consent for processing is not represented in the system."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Unawareness** against `End User`.\n\nMitigation: Provide clear processing notices and capture a lawful basis/consent; expose data-subject rights (access, erasure).\nControls: GDPR-ART13",
                "markdown": "**Unawareness** against `End User`.\n\nMitigation: Provide clear processing notices and capture a lawful basis/consent; expose data-subject rights (access, erasure).\nControls: GDPR-ART13"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Unawareness",
                "cwe": "",
                "owaspTop10": "",
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "L-STORE-LINK",
              "name": "RecordsAreLinkableAcrossContexts(noPseudonymisation)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Records are linkable across contexts (no pseudonymisation)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database stores personal data without pseudonymisation, so records about the same person can be linked across contexts."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Linkability** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Pseudonymise or tokenise identifiers at rest; separate linkable keys from personal data and restrict re-identification.\nControls: GDPR-ART25, NIST-PT-3",
                "markdown": "**Linkability** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Pseudonymise or tokenise identifiers at rest; separate linkable keys from personal data and restrict re-identification.\nControls: GDPR-ART25, NIST-PT-3"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Linkability",
                "cwe": "",
                "owaspTop10": "",
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "D-PROC-RATELIMIT",
              "name": "NoRateLimitingOnAnInternet-facingProcess",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No rate limiting on an internet-facing process"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service is internet-facing without rate limiting or quotas, so it can be overwhelmed by request floods."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Denial of service** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Apply rate limiting, request quotas, timeouts and resource caps; place the service behind an edge/DoS-protection layer.\nControls: ASVS-11.1.4, NIST-SC-5\nWeakness: CWE-770\nOWASP Top 10: A04:2021 - Insecure Design",
                "markdown": "**Denial of service** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Apply rate limiting, request quotas, timeouts and resource caps; place the service behind an edge/DoS-protection layer.\nControls: ASVS-11.1.4, NIST-SC-5\nWeakness: CWE-770\nOWASP Top 10: A04:2021 - Insecure Design"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Denial of service",
                "cwe": "CWE-770",
                "owaspTop10": "A04:2021 - Insecure Design",
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "R-PROC-LOG",
              "name": "Security-relevantActionsAreNotAuditable",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Security-relevant actions are not auditable"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sample Web App Service performs security-relevant actions but does not emit tamper-resistant audit logs, so actors can deny having acted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Repudiation** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Log security-relevant events with user identity, timestamp and outcome to an append-only, access-controlled store.\nControls: ASVS-7.1.3, NIST-AU-2, NIST-AU-9\nWeakness: CWE-778\nOWASP Top 10: A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures",
                "markdown": "**Repudiation** against `Sample Web App Service`.\n\nMitigation: Log security-relevant events with user identity, timestamp and outcome to an append-only, access-controlled store.\nControls: ASVS-7.1.3, NIST-AU-2, NIST-AU-9\nWeakness: CWE-778\nOWASP Top 10: A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Repudiation",
                "cwe": "CWE-778",
                "owaspTop10": "A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures",
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "NC-STORE-RETAIN",
              "name": "NoRetentionGovernanceControlsOnPersonalData(non-compliance)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No retention/governance controls on personal data (non-compliance)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database holds personal data without evidence of retention limits or access auditing, risking non-compliance with storage-limitation duties."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/www-community/Threat_Modeling",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Non-compliance** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Define and enforce retention/deletion schedules, log access to personal data, and document the lawful basis and purpose.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-STORAGE, NIST-SI-12",
                "markdown": "**Non-compliance** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Define and enforce retention/deletion schedules, log access to personal data, and document the lawful basis and purpose.\nControls: GDPR-ART5-STORAGE, NIST-SI-12"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Non-compliance",
                "cwe": "",
                "owaspTop10": "",
                "security-severity": "3.2",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "T-STORE-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "StoredDataCanBeModifiedWithoutDetection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Stored data can be modified without detection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database persists data without integrity controls or change auditing, so unauthorized modification may go unnoticed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/345.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Tampering** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Apply write authorization, integrity checks (hashing/signing) and tamper-evident audit logging to the store.\nControls: ASVS-1.9.2, NIST-SI-7\nWeakness: CWE-345\nOWASP Top 10: A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures",
                "markdown": "**Tampering** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Apply write authorization, integrity checks (hashing/signing) and tamper-evident audit logging to the store.\nControls: ASVS-1.9.2, NIST-SI-7\nWeakness: CWE-345\nOWASP Top 10: A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Tampering",
                "cwe": "CWE-345",
                "owaspTop10": "A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures",
                "security-severity": "3.2",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "D-STORE-EXHAUST",
              "name": "UnboundedGrowthOrConnectionExhaustionInTheStore",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unbounded growth or connection exhaustion in the store"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database can be driven to resource exhaustion (storage, connections) by unbounded writes from upstream processes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Denial of service** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Enforce connection pooling limits, quotas and input size caps upstream; monitor capacity and set alerts.\nControls: NIST-SC-5\nWeakness: CWE-770\nOWASP Top 10: A04:2021 - Insecure Design",
                "markdown": "**Denial of service** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Enforce connection pooling limits, quotas and input size caps upstream; monitor capacity and set alerts.\nControls: NIST-SC-5\nWeakness: CWE-770\nOWASP Top 10: A04:2021 - Insecure Design"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Denial of service",
                "cwe": "CWE-770",
                "owaspTop10": "A04:2021 - Insecure Design",
                "security-severity": "2.4",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "threat-model",
                  "stride"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "R-STORE-LOG",
              "name": "WritesToTheStoreAreNotAttributable",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Writes to the store are not attributable"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite Database does not record who changed what, so repudiation of data changes is possible."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "**Repudiation** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Record attributable, append-only change history for the store and protect it from the accounts that can write data.\nControls: ASVS-7.1.3, NIST-AU-2\nWeakness: CWE-778\nOWASP Top 10: A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures",
                "markdown": "**Repudiation** against `SQLite Database`.\n\nMitigation: Record attributable, append-only change history for the store and protect it from the accounts that can write data.\nControls: ASVS-7.1.3, NIST-AU-2\nWeakness: CWE-778\nOWASP Top 10: A09:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stride": "Repudiation",
                "cwe": "CWE-778",
